## Architecture Notes (Phase 2)
- Role switching is activated when `role_assignment_interval > 0` AND `action_mode == "compound"`
- Role state is stored on trainer._role_states (list of dicts, one per env)
- Generation reads role state from trainer to build role-aware observations and prompts
- Tool results are stored in observation._tool_results dict keyed by (id(env), agent_id)
- Tool results flow: step T generation → _tool_results → pop_tool_result → role_states → step T+1 obs
- Role assignment is NOT part of the trainable trajectory (no gradients, no log-probs)
- When role switching is disabled (interval=0 or text mode), all code paths are unchanged
- Backward compatible: no changes to text mode, existing compound mode without roles unchanged
